  A BlogML export of the endjin blog. BlogML is an engine-to-engine migration format, so what it has to
  carry is everything a blog holds that a syndication feed drops: unapproved authors and comments,
  trackbacks, attachments, category hierarchy, view counts and engine-specific extended properties.

  The unapproved author, comment and trackback are deliberate. BlogMLApprovalStatus has two values and
  an export where everything is approved never exercises the other one — and "approved" is exactly the
  field an importer must not get wrong, because getting it wrong publishes something the author did not.
-->
