    <post id="post-2" date-created="2026-08-06T14:00:00Z" date-modified="2026-08-06T15:00:00Z" approved="true" post-url="https://endjin.com/blog/optimising-dax-formula-engine-and-storage-engine" type="normal" hasexcerpt="false" views="850">
      <title type="text">Optimising DAX: The Formula Engine and Storage Engine</title>
      <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Power BI divides query work between two engines with very different characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Formula Engine&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Single-threaded, and where a slow query usually ends up.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Storage Engine&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Multi-threaded and compressed. Pushing work here is most of what optimisation means.&lt;/p&gt;</content>
